          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "3c240ff4e339d060:part:002"
        },
        {
          "page": 12,
          "section": null,
          "quote": "regions enriched with Ti and Zr are more prone to atomic movement during the deformation, acting as \"soft zones\" in dislocation motion. On the other hand, those regions enriched with Nb, Ta, and Mo act as \"hard zones,\" serving as obstacles for dislocation movements.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "3c240ff4e339d060:part:002"
        }
      ]
    },
